# NVMe Disk Knowledge Comparison Script
# This script evaluates two models' knowledge of NVMe storage technology

# Initialize variables
set model1 = "mistral_1"
set model2 = "nvidia_1"
set technology = "NVMe"
set interface = "PCIe"
set output_dir = ${technology}_storage_comparison
set question_file = ${technology}_questions.txt
set results1 = "mistral_results.txt"
set results2 = "nvidia_results.txt"
set comparison = "comparison_report.txt"
/dump all
#/quit

# Create question file
# Disable session history to prevent cross-model context accumulation
/session history off

/clearfile
/multiline
Please create a comprehensive set of 10 questions about ${technology} disks that would test an AI's knowledge depth and accuracy. Include questions about:

1. Technical specifications and architecture
2. Performance characteristics compared to ${interface} versions
3. Protocol differences from SATA/AHCI
4. Form factor standards (M.2, U.2, EDSFF)
5. NAND flash technology used in ${technology} SSDs
6. Thermal management and power consumption
7. Enterprise vs consumer ${technology} implementations
8. Common performance bottlenecks
9. Security features (TCG Opal, AES encryption)
10. Emerging technologies (CXL, ZNS, KV-SSDs)

Format as numbered questions, one per line.
;;
/multiline
/save ${output_dir}/${question_file}

# Set up output directory (simulated by using different filenames)
/clearfile

# Test Model 1 (mistral_1)
/model ${model1}
/prompt ${output_dir}/${question_file}
/save ${output_dir}/${results1}
/filebank1 ${output_dir}/${results1}

# Test Model 2 (nvidia_1)
/model ${model2}
/prompt ${output_dir}/${question_file}
/save ${output_dir}/${results2}
/filebank2 ${output_dir}/${results2}

# Generate comparison report
/clearfile
/multiline
Analyze the following two sets of responses about ${technology} disks from different AI models.
Compare them for:

1. Technical accuracy of information
2. Depth of engineering knowledge
3. Understanding of protocol specifications
4. Specificity of performance details
5. Recognition of industry standards
6. Handling of form factor differences
7. Any factual errors or omissions

Model 1 (${model1}) responses:
---
{filebank1}
---

Model 2 (${model2}) responses:
---
{filebank2}
---

Provide a detailed comparison with specific examples from each model's responses.
Also give an overall assessment of which model demonstrates better knowledge of ${technology} storage technology and why.
;;
/multiline

# Load the questions and responses into file banks for the comparison
/filebank1 ${output_dir}/${results1}
/filebank2 ${output_dir}/${results2}
/save ${output_dir}/${comparison}
/filebank3 ${output_dir}/${comparison}

/clearfile
/multiline
Create a scoring table (1-10 scale) for each model across these categories:
1. Technical accuracy
2. Protocol knowledge
3. Performance understanding
4. Industry standards expertise
5. Overall technical depth

Based on the comparison report in {filebank3}, fill in the scores and calculate totals.
;;
/multiline
/save ${output_dir}/scores_${model1}_vs_${model2}.txt

# Final summary
/clearfile
/multiline
Based on all the previous analysis, provide a final verdict:
Which model (${model1} or ${model2}) has superior knowledge of ${technology} storage technology?
What are the key strengths of each model's responses?
What recommendations would you make for someone seeking technical information about ${technology} disks?
;;
/multiline
/save ${output_dir}/final_verdict.txt
